WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.909
A couple of new adapted monsters from the
original Scary Stories book trilogy have been

00:00:03.909 --> 00:00:07.779
revealed in the new trailer, so if you want
to hear about those, then stick around -- to

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:08.830
the end of this video.

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:09.830
But first…

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:13.180
I’ve been waiting all winter to hang this
baby back up.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.420
So the new Scary Stories trailer contains
a mix of new footage and stuff we’ve seen

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.900
before in the Super Bowl Teasers.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.560
If you’re sitting there wondering, “why
I haven’t seen that footage; what are you

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.780
talking about?” -- it could be because you’re
not subscribed with deathbell notifications

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:30.400
on?

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:34.460
So the trailer starts, as many movie trailers
do, establishing the setting.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:35.470
1960s.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:36.470
Mill Valley, Pennsylvania.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:40.330
Our characters discover a spooky house and
go inside where we see our first Thing You

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:41.330
Missed.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:45.250
Yeah, we got a counter now, because I ran
a poll and you guys said yeah… might as

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:46.700
well put a counter.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:50.390
The room is lit by candle light -- and this
whole situation is probably a reference to

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:54.470
The Curse, a story from More Scary Stories
To Tell In The Dark, in which some college

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:59.210
kids are doing a frat initiation where they
must explore this deserted house with a candle.

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:02.580
The other students watch from outside where
they see that each pledge who attempts the

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:06.130
dare disappears after their candle goes out
on the third floor.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:09.530
Eventually, they all go up to investigate,
thinking it was some kind of prank, but they

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:13.009
find nothing, with no sign of the disappeared
students.

00:01:13.009 --> 00:01:17.100
Every year since then, a frat member has died
or gone crazy, and the writer of the story

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.340
is the only one left remaining.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:22.900
My guess is that this college initiation was
changed to a high school dare to better fit

00:01:22.909 --> 00:01:24.350
the characters of this movie.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.689
The kids in the movie find this book, and
it seems that the scary stories from the book

00:01:27.689 --> 00:01:29.740
start to come true and haunt their town.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:32.759
I’m guessing this is one of the illustrations
found in that book.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:36.259
Not quite as creepy as some of the illustrations
in the actual book trilogy that this movie

00:01:36.259 --> 00:01:40.539
is based on, but still kind of creepy to find
an old picture containing a headless sailor

00:01:40.539 --> 00:01:41.539
just standing there.

00:01:41.539 --> 00:01:45.030
It looks like they are going to be combining
tales from different stories.

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:48.459
Headlessness is one of the most common themes
found in the books, as someone loses their

00:01:48.459 --> 00:01:52.640
head, literally in six different short stories:
“May I Carry Your Basket”, “Aaron Kelley’s

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:58.490
Bones”, “Oh Susanna”, “The Brown Suit”,
“It’s Him” and the iconic “Me Tie

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:02.889
Doughty Walker”.

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:07.179
But the sailor outfit can only point to one
story called “Somebody Fell From Aloft”,

00:02:07.179 --> 00:02:11.009
about a mysterious body that falls onto a
ship on an oversea voyage.

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:14.599
If you pause on the next image you’ll see
that “May I Carry Your Basket” and “Somebody

00:02:14.599 --> 00:02:18.349
Fell From Aloft” are next to each other
in the movie version of the book, despite

00:02:18.349 --> 00:02:20.850
the fact that they aren’t even in the same
book in real life.

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:24.950
There’s one short story that’s generally
regarded the highest by fans, and that is

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:28.530
“Harold”, the tale of two farmers who
make a scarecrow and name it after another

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:30.340
farmer, Harold, that they don’t like.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:33.610
The Scarecrow becomes a punching bag for them
whenever they needed to let off some steam,

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:38.209
but eventually start to notice that Harold
is making grunting noises, growing, and eventually

00:02:38.209 --> 00:02:41.819
walking around on their roof and deskinning
his victims.

00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:46.459
The trailer shows the ominous cornfield, Harold
possibly watching one of the farmers and Harold’s

00:02:46.459 --> 00:02:51.210
angry expression as his face crawls with cockroaches
-- this looks like it’s going to be even

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.810
creepier than the story that it’s based
on.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:56.689
Another story I think we’ll see is called
“The Bed By The Window”.

00:02:56.689 --> 00:03:00.450
In the trailer, we see the kids approaching
this hospital, and in the story, patients

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.950
who have the bed next to the window keep dying.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:06.540
One man who moves into the bed keeps describing
how amazing the window view is -- so this

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.150
other guy named George ends up murdering him
in his sleep so that he can move into the

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:14.549
bed with the window view, but when he gets
there, all he can see is a brick wall.

00:03:14.549 --> 00:03:17.819
Since the movie is going to be combining stories,
I think the hallway scene where we see the

00:03:17.819 --> 00:03:21.491
Pale Skinned Lady from “The Dream” could
be at that same hospital -- I believe in the

00:03:21.491 --> 00:03:24.010
last video I speculated that it might have
been their high school.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:27.750
By the way, if you want to hear my analysis
of The Pale Skinned Lady, The Big Toe Creature,

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:32.230
The Red Spot or The Gangly Boi, I go more
in depth about those in my Scary Stories Teaser

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:34.739
Analysis video, which you can check out here.

00:03:34.739 --> 00:03:38.420
The trailer also features a police officer
character, which is probably a smart choice

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:41.549
considering that there are at least five stories
in the books where cops get involved.

00:03:41.549 --> 00:03:44.680
There’s “High Beams”, in which they
arrest a man found hiding in the back of a

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:48.319
girl’s truck with a knife; “The Babysitter”,
in which they arrest an intruder hiding in

00:03:48.319 --> 00:03:52.030
an attic; “The Viper” in which a paranoid
man alerts the police of some suspicious phone

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:56.439
calls but it turns out to be a German janitor
who vants to vipe his vindows…

00:03:56.439 --> 00:03:59.369
...by the looks of things I could use a Viper
right about now myself…

00:03:59.369 --> 00:04:03.379
... then there’s “The Window”, not to
be confused by the previously mentioned “The

00:04:03.379 --> 00:04:07.099
Bed By The Window”, where police are called
after a vampire breaks into someone’s house

00:04:07.099 --> 00:04:11.500
through the window even though that’s not
allowed with vampires; and finally, “The

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:12.500
Trouble”.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:15.239
This one has the most police involvement -- it’s
about a house that is seemingly possessed

00:04:15.239 --> 00:04:19.549
by a Poltergeist and the stubborn detective
tries his best to find a rational explanation

00:04:19.549 --> 00:04:20.789
for everything that's happened.

00:04:20.789 --> 00:04:25.030
This cop’s jailhouse looks to play a significant
role as the home of the monster from “The

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:26.030
Thing.”

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:29.880
The characters in that story describe a strange
creature crawling out of a turnip field.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:34.540
At first it looks like some kind of weird
animal, but then they realize it is vaguely

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.540
human.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.960
This might be the creepiest image in the trailer
actually if you slow it down and get a good

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:40.240
look at this The Thing’s face.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:44.380
I’m sure there will probably be some weirdo
in the comments though who thinks he’s cute...

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:45.479
“Who’s a good boy?”

00:04:45.479 --> 00:04:48.500
There’s one more new creature at the very
end of the trailer.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:51.800
Now there are several ghosts throughout the
series, but I think this is the ghost from

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:54.220
“The Haunted House”, a story from the
first book.

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:57.280
It’s about a preacher who tries to put an
uneasy spirit to rest.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:01.080
He hears murderous sounds within the house,
before the ghost eventually approaches him

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:04.830
and tells the story of how her lover killed
her for her money and hid her body in the

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:05.830
cellar.

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:09.180
She wants him to give her a proper burial
and use her detached finger to find the her

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:10.180
killer.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:13.430
He puts the finger in the collection plate
at church, and it sticks to the man who murdered

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:14.430
her.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:17.900
He confesses to his crimes, and so the ghost
tells the preacher where to find the hidden

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:18.900
money.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:22.370
But the spot where the ghost initially grabbed
his coat has her finger marks permanently

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:23.669
burned into the cloth.

00:05:23.669 --> 00:05:27.370
I’m going to keep you up to date on any
things you might have missed in future teasers

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:29.880
and trailers for Scary Stories to Tell In
The Dark.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:31.400
By the way, how many was that?.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.860
Ohh okay, so that’s how many there were.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:36.360
No more comments questioning the number of
Things You Missed.

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:39.289
That just leaves the comments saying “you
don’t know what I missed -- how dare you

00:05:39.289 --> 00:05:40.360
assume what I missed.”

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:44.360
If you haven’t seen the video on the left,
watch that to see about the other creatures

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:49.580
that I didn’t cover in this video, and remember
to subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:55.379
week -- ring that deathbell for notifications,
and I’ll see you in the next episode, assuming

00:05:55.379 --> 00:05:56.370
we both survive.

